---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import InvestmentCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/InvestmentCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="investment-calculator">
  <InvestmentCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the investment calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The investment calculator grows a starting amount and a fixed monthly deposit at a yearly return
      compounded monthly. The balance is <code>FV = P × (1 + i)^n + PMT × ((1 + i)^n − 1) ÷ i</code>, where
      <code>P</code> is the starting amount, <code>PMT</code> is the monthly deposit, <code>i</code> is the
      yearly return divided by 12 and <code>n</code> is the number of months. With deposits at the start of
      each month, the deposit part is multiplied by <code>(1 + i)</code>, because each deposit earns one
      more month.
    </p>
    <p>
      Growth is the balance minus the money you put in. The value in today's money is
      <code>FV ÷ (1 + inflation)^years</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      10,000 to start and 500 at the end of each month for 20 years at 7% grows to 300,851. You put in
      130,000, so 170,851 is growth. At 2.5% inflation that balance is worth 183,600 in today's money. With
      deposits at the start of each month the balance is 302,370.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The return is the same every month. Real markets go up and down, and the order of good and bad years
      changes the result. Fees and taxes are not included, so enter a return after fees.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
